→   - Evidence: These likely all refer to De Lacey, the blind father in the cottage\n    61→   - Location: Alias resolution for descriptive references\n    62→   - Fix: Improve resolution of descriptive phrases (\"the old man\") to canonical names\n    63→\n    64→8. **Character split: \"Father\" vs \"my father\"**\n    65→   - Problem: \"Father\" (6 mentions) listed separately from \"my father\" (46 mentions)\n    66→   - Evidence: These are the same character (Alphonse Frankenstein) with different article usage\n    67→   - Location: Canonical name selection\n    68→   - Fix: Normalize \"my X\" and \"X\" and \"the X\" before creating separate entries\n    69→\n    70→### LOW\n    71→9. **Profile confidence issues**\n    72→   - Problem: Elizabeth and Margaret have low confidence (0.30) due to JSON parsing failures\n    73→   - Evidence: Mentioned in pipeline notes\n    74→   - Location: Profile generation LLM output parsing\n    75→   - Fix: Improve JSON extraction robustness or prompt engineering\n    76→\n    77→## Fix History\n    78→### Attempt 1: Fixed CLI output path handling\n    79→**Issue:** CLI ignored explicit `--html` and `--output` flags, creating timestamped directory instead\n    80→\n    81→**Fix Applied:**\n    82→- Modified `src/cli.py` lines 367-368: Added `output_path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)` for JSON output\n    83→- Modified `src/cli.py` lines 397-398: Added `html_path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)` for HTML output\n    84→\n    85→**Testing:** All 444 tests pass.\n    86→\n    87→### Attempt 2: Enhanced alias candidate pair generation for relational descriptors\n    88→**Issue:** Critical #1, #2, #8 - Relational/familial descriptors like \"my father\", \"Father\" not being paired with proper names like \"Alphonse Frankenstein\" for alias resolution\n    89→\n    90→**Root Cause:** The `_candidate_pairs_for_merge` function in `src/pipeline/character_extraction/consensus.py` only generated candidate pairs based on